course: dictionary
lesson: 5141
title: Iodine and the starch test
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists often need to find out if a substance is present, and they use a test that changes colour. «Plant cells have a stiff wall, a nucleus and, in green parts, chloroplasts that catch light; iodine stain makes the nucleus show as a dark dot.» Here the iodine stain is a tool that makes a hidden part easy to see.
explain: Iodine is also the name of a chemical element with the symbol I. In the starch test, iodine solution starts orange-brown. If starch is present, the solution turns blue-black. The colour change tells you the starch is there.
explain: Iodine is also used as a brown liquid on cuts to kill germs. Doctors and nurses call this an antiseptic. Iodine is also a mineral your body needs in tiny amounts, which is why salt is sometimes iodised.
fact: «Iodine» is a chemical element with the symbol I and the number 53.
fact: When iodine is heated, it gives off a violet gas.
fact: Iodine solution turns blue-black when starch is present.
fact: Iodine is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say some iodine, not two iodines.
fact: The body needs a little iodine to make hormones, and it is found in fish, seaweed, milk and iodised salt.
exercise: «Plant cells have a stiff wall, a nucleus and, in green parts, chloroplasts that catch light; iodine stain makes the nucleus show as a dark dot.» What does the iodine stain make the nucleus show as? | A bright green ring | A violet gas | *A dark dot | A stiff wall
exercise: A brown liquid is put on a cut to kill germs. What is it? | *Iodine | Milk | Sugar water | Seaweed
exercise: In the starch test, what colour does iodine solution turn when starch is present? | Orange-brown, no change | Bright white | *Blue-black | Violet
test: Iodine is a mineral the body needs in tiny amounts. Which food is a good source of iodine? | *Fish | Sugar | Chalk | Plain water
test: What is the symbol for the chemical element iodine? | Io | *I | Ir | Id
exam: When iodine is heated, it gives off a violet gas. What is the number of iodine in the periodic table? | 45 | *53 | 35 | 63
